        "original_id": "5880d31f-a44c-5e69-9145-07a0b2275e4c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Daniel Craig, Terence Gross, Toni Collette, Stephen Tompkinson, Joseph Stalin\n- Films: Hotel Splendide, Casino Royale, Archangel, Brassed Off\n- Roles: James Bond, Dr. Christopher \"Fluke\" Kelso\n- Topics: British independent dark comedy, Soviet history\n\nFacts:\n- Stephen Tompkinson starred in the film Brassed Off in 1996.\n- Hotel Splendide is a 2000 British independent dark comedy film written and directed by Terence Gross and starring Toni Collette and Daniel Craig.\n- Stephen Tompkinson also starred in the 2000 film Hotel Splendide.\n- In the 2005 film Archangel, Daniel Craig plays Dr. Christopher \"Fluke\" Kelso, an English expert on Soviet history who is in Moscow for a conference on Joseph Stalin.\n- Daniel Craig was cast as James Bond in October 2005.\n- Daniel Craig's first James Bond film, Casino Royale, was released internationally in November 2006.",
